<section id="top">
        <div class="page-shell about-page-intro">
            <span class="eyebrow">Quickler in Australia</span>
            <h1>No-app site inspections for Australian field teams.</h1>
            <p class="page-lede">Picture a crew arriving on a regional site at first light: an excavator and a couple of utes to check over, a pre-start to complete, and a supervisor back in the depot who needs to know everything is good to run. Quickler replaces the clipboard and the half-loaded tablet app with a WhatsApp conversation. The operator answers the pre-start questions by text, voice note or photo on the phone already in their pocket, and the supervisor sees a clean digital record before the machine turns a wheel.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="content-duo">
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">The pre-start scenario</p>
                        <h2>From clipboard to chat, before the plant starts.</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>Paper pre-starts get rained on, left in the cab, or filled in from memory at the end of the day. A tablet app means a device to charge, log in to, and hand around the crew. Neither suits a team spread across sites who change daily. Quickler runs the same check as a guided chat.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>The operator opens WhatsApp and works through the pre-start one question at a time</li>
                        <li>A cracked guard or a low hydraulic level is logged with a photo on the spot</li>
                        <li>Voice notes capture a quick observation without typing in the cold</li>
                        <li>A defect flags the item amber or red so the supervisor sees it immediately</li>
                        <li>If nothing is wrong, the all-clear is logged in under a minute</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Because there is no app to install and no per-user fee, a labour-hire operator or a new subbie completes a compliant check the first time they are sent the chat. No onboarding, no licence to assign.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="section-frame">
                <div class="section-header">
                    <div>
                        <p class="section-label">What the supervisor gets</p>
                        <h2>A live record, not a shoebox of paper.</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="detail-body">
                    <p>Every completed inspection lands as a structured digital record on a dashboard, not as a photo of a form in a group chat. The supervisor reads the whole fleet at a glance.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Red, amber and green status across every machine, vehicle and site</li>
                        <li>Open faults stay visible until they are closed out, with the photo evidence attached</li>
                        <li>Each answer sits against the right question, so nothing is lost in a thread</li>
                        <li>A PDF can be exported when a client, an insurer or a records file needs a document</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>The digital record is the source of truth and is searchable later; the PDF is there when paperwork is genuinely required, rather than being the whole point of the exercise.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

